WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:13.815
Tina: What do you mean, “It’s not from this world”?

2
00:00:13.816 --> 00:00:15.926
Brad: It’s not from this world.

3
00:00:15.927 --> 00:00:17.576
I checked the Internet.

4
00:00:17.577 --> 00:00:20.400
Brad: We don’t have clay like that.

5
00:00:20.401 --> 00:00:24.764
Danny: I told you I was telling the truth!

6
00:00:24.765 --> 00:00:30.015
Tina: So this clay was given to you . . . by a giant?

7
00:00:30.016 --> 00:00:32.800
Danny: I told you his name is Hopian.

8
00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:35.512
Brad: And what are you supposed to do?

9
00:00:35.513 --> 00:00:40.209
Danny: We’re supposed to help bring back the lost color to his world!

10
00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:43.008
Tina: And how are we going to do this?

11
00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:45.350
Danny: He told me to remember something.

12
00:00:45.351 --> 00:00:51.363
Danny: He said, “Your imagination can unlock any door.”

13
00:00:51.364 --> 00:00:54.173
Tina: Your imagination?

14
00:00:54.174 --> 00:00:55.686
Danny: Yes.

15
00:00:55.687 --> 00:00:58.178
Brad: Can unlock any door?

16
00:00:58.179 --> 00:00:59.797
Danny: Yes.

17
00:00:59.798 --> 00:01:01.890
Brad: What does that mean?

18
00:01:01.891 --> 00:01:05.233
Danny: I don’t know!

19
00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:08.099
Tina: This is crazy.

20
00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.858
Brad: Wait a second.

21
00:01:09.859 --> 00:01:12.733
It’s got to be some sort of riddle.

22
00:01:12.734 --> 00:01:13.960
Tina: And?

23
00:01:13.961 --> 00:01:19.553
Brad: My computer can solve any problem.

24
00:01:19.554 --> 00:01:24.303
Danny: So what does it say?

25
00:01:24.304 --> 00:01:27.121
Brad: Maybe I’m not putting it in right.

26
00:01:27.122 --> 00:01:29.769
Tina: Any answer is better than nothing.

27
00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:34.538
What does it say?

28
00:01:34.539 --> 00:01:39.341
Brad: “Every door is different.”

29
00:01:39.342 --> 00:01:45.636
Tina: Hey, I’ve got an idea.

30
00:01:45.637 --> 00:01:51.107
Tina: Maybe if we look at it long enough, we’ll figure it out.

31
00:01:51.108 --> 00:01:53.632
Brad: I can barely read that.

32
00:01:53.633 --> 00:01:56.487
Tina: You know what it says!

33
00:01:56.488 --> 00:02:02.522
Danny: Hey, don’t fight.

34
00:02:02.523 --> 00:02:04.932
Maybe it’s up to me.

35
00:02:04.933 --> 00:02:08.196
Tina: He did say, “Your imagination.”

36
00:02:08.197 --> 00:02:11.868
Brad: And you have this special clay to help. Right?

37
00:02:11.869 --> 00:02:14.369
Danny: That’s it!

38
00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:15.688
Tina: What’s it?

39
00:02:15.689 --> 00:02:20.440
Danny: Stand back and watch!

40
00:02:20.441 --> 00:02:26.288
Brad: Oh great. Who are you? Harry Potter?

41
00:02:26.289 --> 00:02:35.310
Danny: ALA KAZAAM KABLAM, TAKE ME TO GINORMOUS!

42
00:02:35.311 --> 00:02:37.708
Brad: Um . . . didn’t work.

43
00:02:37.709 --> 00:02:40.412
Tina: We’re still in the bushes, Danny.

44
00:02:40.413 --> 00:02:47.009
Danny: My imagination isn’t that great, I guess.

45
00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:50.273
Brad: Only two more minutes of recess left!

46
00:02:50.274 --> 00:02:59.050
Tina: Yeah, we don’t want to be late. Let’s go!

47
00:02:59.051 --> 00:03:01.044
Danny: What’s that sound?

48
00:03:01.045 --> 00:03:04.143
Tina: It’s just my keys. Hurry!

49
00:03:04.144 --> 00:03:06.857
Danny: WAIT!
